        <mxCell id="notes_body" value="• Each layer box is filled with its OPERATING zone colour (the zone the layer receives). The arrow leaving the layer is labelled with the PRODUCED zone (the zone the request is in after the layer fires).&#10;&#10;• L1 and L2 both operate in Z0 (filled red). L2 produces Z1 (TLS-terminated edge perimeter). L3 operates in Z1 (filled yellow) and produces Z2. L4 produces Z3. L5 stays in Z3 (gating only, no zone crossing). L6 produces Z4 — the envelope crossing per ADR-0003. L7 operates entirely within Z4.&#10;&#10;• L8 sits beside the stack. Agents and automation runtimes do NOT have a back-channel into L7; they traverse the same L1 → L2 → L3 → … chain as a human user. The dashed grey arrow re-entering at L1 makes this rule visible. Per ADR-0002, agents are clients.&#10;&#10;• The 🔒 marker on the L6 → L7 arrow is a placeholder for the workspace-specific seal stencil that will ship in Phase C.2 (full template set).&#10;&#10;• This diagram is workspace-canonical and intentionally vendor-neutral. Profile-specific diagrams (e.g., self-hosted-vps deployment topology) belong in their own files." vertex="1" parent="1" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontColor=#444444;whiteSpace=wrap;">
          <mxGeometry x="700" y="1214" width="640" height="240" as="geometry"/>
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="footer" value="Source: architecture/control-layers.md · architecture/security-boundaries.md · ADR-0001 (eight-layer model) · ADR-0002 (agents-as-clients) · ADR-0003 (internal identity envelope)&#10;Last reviewed: 2026-05-28 by @mikegtech · Next review: 2026-08-28 · Diagram ID: eight-layer-control-model · Workspace style library: architecture/diagrams/styles/workspace.drawio" vertex="1" parent="1" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=12;fontColor=#444444;whiteSpace=wrap;">
